  "q0": "The group did not ultimately decide to remove the curve. The Project Manager suggested removing the curve as a cost-saving option, but it was rejected because it would make the remote control too ordinary and less distinctive. The group instead decided to keep the curve to maintain the product's unique, trendy appearance and differentiate it from standard remote controls.",
  "q1": "The group discussed several product name options, including 'Banana Remote,' 'R_C_Deluxe,' 'Real Reaction,' and 'Triple R.' After debate, they agreed on 'Triple R' as the final name. It was chosen for being short, catchy, and aligned with the brand name 'Real Reaction,' while avoiding confusion or unappealing associations like 'banana' or 'deluxe.'",
  "q2": "The group discussed removing speech recognition and the special yellow color to reduce production costs from 17 euros to 12.5 euros, which was the budget limit. They decided to scrap speech recognition due to lower customer preference and higher cost, and to replace the special color with a standard black and grey option. The group also considered removing the rubber material or the curve, but ultimately kept the rubber for its durability and the curve for its distinctive, trendy feel.",
  "q3": "The advantage of 'triple R' over 'triple RC' was that 'triple R' sounded more cohesive and was perceived as a unified, branded name. The group felt 'triple RC' sounded like it combined two different things (remote and control) and was less intuitive. 'Triple R' was seen as more stylish, memorable, and aligned with the brand identity of 'Real Reaction,' making it more appealing for product branding."
}

